            <path class="sp" d="M1.5 24v8M7.5 19v18M13.5 13v30M19.5 17v22M25.5 9v38M31.5 5v46M37.5 14v28M43.5 20v16M49.5 11v34M55.5 6v44M61.5 16v24M67.5 22v12M73.5 15v26M79.5 8v40M85.5 12v32M91.5 19v18M97.5 23v10"/>
            <g class="gap"><rect class="cut" x="101" y="5" width="47" height="46" rx="9"/><path class="si" d="M103.5 28v.01M109.5 28v.01M115.5 28v.01M121.5 28v.01M127.5 28v.01M133.5 28v.01M139.5 28v.01M145.5 28v.01"/></g>
            <g class="b"><path class="sp" d="M151.5 22v12M157.5 15v26M163.5 7v42M169.5 11v34M175.5 18v20M181.5 10v36M187.5 4v48M193.5 13v30M199.5 21v14M205.5 16v24M211.5 9v38M217.5 5v46M223.5 14v28M229.5 19v18M235.5 12v32M241.5 17v22M247.5 23v10"/>
              <g class="gap"><rect class="cut" x="251" y="5" width="53" height="46" rx="9"/><path class="si" d="M253.5 28v.01M259.5 28v.01M265.5 28v.01M271.5 28v.01M277.5 28v.01M283.5 28v.01M289.5 28v.01M295.5 28v.01M301.5 28v.01"/></g></g>
            <g class="c"><path class="sp" d="M307.5 23v10M313.5 17v22M319.5 10v36M325.5 4v48M331.5 12v32M337.5 19v18M343.5 14v28M349.5 7v42M355.5 15v26M361.5 21v14M367.5 11v34M373.5 6v44M379.5 9v38M385.5 18v20M391.5 13v30M397.5 5v46M403.5 16v24M409.5 20v16M415.5 24v8"/></g>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="shot ui low"><span class="pane"><img src="/assets/app-editor.jpg" alt="The timeline: four cut pieces, a captions lane, and lanes for zooms and effects" loading="lazy" width="2400" height="1570"></span></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card rise">
        <div><h3>Captions on every word</h3><p>Big and readable, with the word you're saying lit up. It will mishear a word now and then. Retype it and move on.</p></div>
        <div class="shot"><div class="duo"><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/frame-1.jpg" alt="Caption: HATE CUTTING" loading="lazy" width="720" height="1280"></div><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/frame-tips.jpg" alt="A second reel, filmed at a desk, with the caption HOOK FIRST" loading="lazy" width="720" height="1280"></div></div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card rise">
        <div><h3>Zooms, emojis, sound and effects</h3><p>Punch in on the line that matters. Pop an emoji. Add a whoosh if you must. There are 7 transitions, 13 picture effects and 19 sounds in there, and I'd use about three of them per reel.</p></div>
        <div class="shot"><div class="duo"><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/frame-5.jpg" alt="A colour-split effect on the clip" loading="lazy" width="720" height="1280"></div><div class="phone"><img src="/assets/frame-6.jpg" alt="A zoom with a party emoji" loading="lazy" width="720" height="1280"></div></div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card rise">
        <div><h3>All your reels in one place</h3><p>New clips wait in an inbox. Start a reel from one, or drop it into a reel you already have as b-roll.</p></div>
        <div class="shot ui"><span class="pane"><img src="/assets/app-list.jpg" alt="The reel list: two finished reels with their pictures and lengths, and a new clip waiting" loading="lazy" width="2400" height="1570"></span></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card rise" id="ai">
        <div>
          <h3>Easy to use with Claude and ChatGPT</h3>
          <p>The first time you open ReelsEasy it asks which one you use: Claude Code, or Codex from the makers of ChatGPT. It opens that one in your reel folder, and from then on you just type what you want. Anything you moved by hand stays where you put it.</p>
          <div class="say">
            <div>Edit the new clip in my inbox into a reel.</div>
            <div>Zoom in on "hate cutting clips" and add a whoosh.</div>
            <div>Show the laptop clip in a corner while I say "so I built an app".</div>
          </div>
          <p class="fine">I built ReelsEasy with Claude Code, so that is the one I have tried. Codex should work the same way. Tell me if it doesn't.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="shot ui"><span class="pane"><img src="/assets/app-setup.jpg" alt="ReelsEasy on first launch, asking: Do you edit with an AI? with buttons for Claude, ChatGPT (Codex) and Not now" loading="lazy" width="2400" height="1570"></span></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
